Package: xios-kde
Name: Xios Desktop (KDE Plasma)
Version: 0.1.15
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Section: Desktop
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 16.5), xios-core (>= 0.1.6), iosc (>= 0.9.36), xios-session (>= 1.0.72), xios-desktop-theme, libjpeg62-turbo (>= 3.1.1+ios1), kwin (>= 6.1.5+ios30), breeze (>= 6.1.5+ios2), plasma-workspace (>= 6.1.5+ios12), plasma-desktop (>= 6.1.5+ios9), plasma-mobile (>= 6.1.5+ios23), plasma-nano (>= 6.1.5+ios3), systemsettings (>= 6.1.5+ios8), kscreen (>= 6.1.5+ios2), powerdevil (>= 6.1.5+ios1), kf6-kded (>= 6.3.0+ios2), qt6-wayland, kf6-breeze-icons, konsole (>= 24.08.0+ios1), dolphin (>= 24.08.0+ios1), kate (>= 24.08.0+ios4), kwrite (>= 24.08.0+ios3), kcalc (>= 24.08.0+ios1), okular (>= 24.08.0+ios3), ark (>= 24.08.0+ios1), gwenview (>= 24.08.0+ios1)
MinimumOSVersion: 16.5.0
Description: KDE Plasma desktop and mobile flavors for Xios
 KDE Plasma on KWin, rendered on the iPad GPU through the iosc compositor
 and ANGLE. Pulls in the Qt 6 runtime, the KDE Frameworks 6 subset Plasma
 needs, KWin, Plasma Desktop, Plasma Mobile/Nano, System Settings, KScreen,
 PowerDevil, and the shared Xios theme assets used by both shells.
 .
 Every KDE app ported so far comes with it, so the desktop is usable the
 moment it finishes installing: Konsole (terminal), Dolphin (files), Kate and
 KWrite (editors), KCalc, Okular (documents), Ark (archives), and Gwenview
 (images).
 .
 Installing this package is the whole setup: open the Xios app afterwards
 and the Plasma session starts.
 .
 Needs iOS 16.5 or newer on a rootless jailbreak (/var/jb); the floor comes
 from KWin's DRM/GBM library chain (libdrm2, libgbm1, libdisplay-info1).
